WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
Speaker 1: Let's take a look at the&nbsp;
continued downfall of Ron DeSantis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:10.980
the Republican Florida governor who is polling&nbsp;
about 20% in the Republican primary, more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:17.820
everybody but Trump, but with seemingly no path&nbsp;
to actually securing the Republican nomination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:25.320
Ron DeSantis was interviewed by Fox News's Stuart&nbsp;
Varney or Fox Business's Stuart Varney. This is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:31.560
Kafka esque moment. I apologize. I apologize.&nbsp;
It is Kafkaesque. Stuart Varney mentions two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:37.440
dissenters. Listen, you're down over 30. How are&nbsp;
you going to catch up? What's your strategy? And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:43.980
DeSantis just attacks the media. I don't know&nbsp;
that this strategy has winner written all over it.&nbsp;

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.769
Speaker 2: You're down.
Speaker 1: Over 30.&nbsp;

00:00:45.769 --> 00:00:48.720
Speaker 4: Points to Trump.
Speaker 2: What's your strategy for catching up?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.460
Well, first, I think it's pretty clear that the&nbsp;
media does not want me to be the candidate. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.320
think that they've tried to create a narrative&nbsp;
that somehow the race is over. This is going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.720
a state by state contest. We've worked really hard&nbsp;
to build tons of organization in places like Iowa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.580
New Hampshire, South Carolina, that you need to&nbsp;
actually be able to win these early contests. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.720
we're going to continue doing that. We've got a&nbsp;
lot of work, but we've had very, very favorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.600
response and we're going to keep building off that&nbsp;
momentum at the end of the day. I think the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.269
that I'm the one that's targeted by the media,&nbsp;
by the left, even by the president of Mexico.&nbsp;

00:01:26.269 --> 00:01:31.560
Speaker 1: Listen, if the strategy is I'm going&nbsp;
to pretend to be a victim just like Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.760
it pretends to be a victim. I guess&nbsp;
he's doing it. But I don't know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.880
this is going to get him too many votes.
Speaker 2: Because people know that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.020
will beat Biden and they know that I will&nbsp;
actually deliver on all these issues and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.440
beat the Democrats at the border. Beat up folks.
Speaker 1: This is really low energy. You're down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.500
32. TRUMP What's your strategy for catching&nbsp;
up? Well, it's mostly the media's fault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:01.260
but I'm going to beat Biden. Well, you're not even&nbsp;
going to face Biden unless you figure out a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:07.500
make up a 30 point gap on Donald Trump. If I want&nbsp;
to be as charitable as possible to Ron DeSantis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:14.820
he seems to be saying when he says it's a state by&nbsp;
state contest. 30 points nationally don't matter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:21.720
If I can win Iowa and or New Hampshire and justify&nbsp;
staying in this race, it's not looking like he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.100
win Iowa or New Hampshire. But let's put that&nbsp;
aside if I want to generously say that's his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.480
strategy. Okay. I guess that's a strategy, which&nbsp;
is forget about the national polling. Just focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:37.620
